<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: RUGBY UNION-WESTERN SAMOA BEAT MUNSTER 35-25.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-WESTERN SAMOA BEAT MUNSTER 35-25.</headline>
<dateline>CORK, Ireland 1996-11-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Samoa beat Munster</p>
<p>35-25 (halftime 18-10) in a rugby union tour match on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Munster - Tries: Mike Lynch (2), penalty try. Conversions:</p>
<p>Aidan O'Halloran (2). Penalties: O'Halloran (2)</p>
<p>Western Samoa - Tries: Terry Fanolua (2), Mark Fatialofa,</p>
<p>Pailate Fili, Sene Ta'ala. Conversions: Fa'avaivai Tanoai (2).</p>
<p>Penalties: Tanoai (2).</p>
</text>
